# The decision rule
## Expected value = p(churn) x save rate x value - (offer + contact cost)

- Contact only customers with positive expected value
- Optimiser picks customer and offer within budget, one offer each, max {{ cfg.campaign.max_contact_share | pct(0) }} contacted
- Four offers with eligibility rules: credit, contract upgrade, service bundle, loyalty reward
- All costs and save rates are visible, sourced assumptions

Notes: Worked example: a customer paying 70 dollars a month is worth about {{ worked_example.value | usd }}; at 60% risk the standard offer is worth {{ worked_example.ev | usd(2) }}. Save rates are deliberately below the 30% literature convention because risky customers are not always responsive.

