# How robust is it?
![](../figures/tornado.png)

- Break-even save rate {{ be.break_even_default_save_rate | pct }} (assumed {{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }})
- Pessimistic {{ scenarios.pessimistic.expected_net_value | usd }} (no campaign) / base {{ scenarios.base.expected_net_value | usd }} / optimistic {{ scenarios.optimistic.expected_net_value | usd }}
- Below {{ be.minimum_viable_save_rate | pct }} save rate: run no campaign

Notes: The save rate and the value horizon dominate. A re-optimised plan never loses money because it drops customers whose value turns negative; a list frozen under pessimistic assumptions would lose {{ (-scenarios.pessimistic.fixed_expected_net_value) | usd }}. This is why we recommend measuring the save rate before scaling.

